I walk further into the market.
There I see an old stall.
An elderly vendor sits there.
On top of the stall's counter, there are some old things.
Near me is a small brass bell.
"Sir, this bell is beautiful," I say.
"What is its price?" I ask.
The elderly vendor says, "That bell is three hundred rupees."
Then I look up.
There is a beautiful wooden box there.
"That box is very old," I say.
Looking at that box, I think.
Five months ago, I came to Mumbai.
Five months ago, everything here was new for me.
Now, I am looking at things in the market here.
"How many rupees is that box?" I ask.
The vendor says, "That box is five hundred rupees."
I smile.
"Thank you," I say.
I do not buy anything, and I walk on.
